{"name":"Oyster Bisque","hex":"#f2e5b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oyster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain marine bivalve mollusks, especially those of the family Ostreidae (the true oysters), usually found adhering to rocks or other fixed objects in shallow water along the seacoasts, or in brackish water in the mouth of rivers.","The delicate oyster-shaped morsel of dark meat contained in a small cavity of the bone on each side of the lower part of the back of a fowl."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale beige colour tinted with grey or pink, like that of an oyster."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oyster"},{"term":"bisque","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick creamy soup made from fish, shellfish, meat or vegetables.","A pale pinkish brown colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale pinkish brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bisque"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oyster","blocks":[{"text":"Oyster is the common name for a number of different families of salt-water bivalve molluscs that live in marine or brackish habitats. In some species, the valves are highly calcified, and many are somewhat irregular in shape. Many oysters are in the superfamily Ostreoidea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg/330px-Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster","wikidata":"Q107411"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Oyster_dubai.jpg/500px-Oyster_dubai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Oyster_dubai.jpg/1280px-Oyster_dubai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped